00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:02,520
You could do it.

161
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:04,480
But yeah, as I said, in the real world,

162
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:07,680
there's always a continuous variable for fixed versus sunk.

163
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:10,320
It's not actually either or.

164
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:12,240
It's not actually binary.

165
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,880
All right, but now,

166
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:16,800
imagine that we have a simultaneous decision

167
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,600
to incurs on costs.

168
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:19,880
Now, we can think about this

169
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,840
in terms of the following normal form.

170
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:24,080
Switching pens.

171
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,400
So, suppose we've got two firms.

172
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:37,320
They can both be in or out.

173
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:39,400
In or out.

174
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,640
So, now, there's no longer any incumbent

175
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,520
because it's two firms

176
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:47,280
that are both deciding whether to enter.

177
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:48,920
And now, we can think about it like this.

178
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:50,040
So, now, if they both enter,

179
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:52,480
as we established, they both are at minus A.

180
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,160
Because if they both enter,

181
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:57,120
then competition drives price down to marginal cost

182
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:00,160
and then they both lose their sunk costs.

183
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,520
Now, if you enter,

184
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:04,080
if firm one enters and the other one doesn't,

185
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:06,240
then firm one will earn the monopoly profit

186
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,720
and the other firm will earn.

187
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:09,560
Firm two earns nothing.

188
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:12,760
If firm two stays out and firm one enters,

189
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:14,640
then it's firm one earns nothing

190
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:16,360
and firm two earns the monopoly profit.

191
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,560
And of course, if they both stay out,

192
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,520
they both get zero.

193
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,560
And this is a normal form,

194
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:23,720
but a lot like the one that we've seen before.

195
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:25,080
Now, if you look for the pure strategy

196
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:25,920
in Nash Equilibria,

